pack habitat-boundary
generation control-1
provenance product topology separation, 2026-08-26; existing packs/habitat-human-factors
authority asserted
note This pack establishes Habitat's product boundary and namespace only. It is deliberately not an implementation. Its purpose is to remove Habitat's dependency on being a Bonfyre administrative surface and give it an independent product identity.

product hab:habitat
  namespace bonfyre/habitat
  display_name Habitat
  kind standalone-product
  state SEEDED
  populated_by packs/habitat-human-factors
  world LIVE
  detail A standalone social and spatial experiment. Not another Bonfyre admin surface and not a visualization of the estate.

subject_family hab:people
  display_name People
  state DECLARED
subject_family hab:groups
  display_name Groups
  state DECLARED
subject_family hab:spaces
  display_name Spaces
  state DECLARED
subject_family hab:occurrences
  display_name Occurrences
  state DECLARED
subject_family hab:experiments
  display_name Experiments
  state DECLARED

reuses AddressPlane
reuses relationship graph
reuses Occurrence
reuses Automerge
reuses Iroh
reuses MoQ
reuses ObjectFabric
reuses media Powers
reuses Vec and Embed
reuses Model Commons
reuses ActivityPub and Matrix

vocabulary person
vocabulary friend
vocabulary member
vocabulary host
vocabulary guest
vocabulary group
vocabulary space
vocabulary presence
vocabulary invite
vocabulary shared
vocabulary private
vocabulary public
vocabulary temporary

invariant Habitat's product language is social; client, tenant, invoice and managed institution do not appear in it
invariant Habitat shares Bonfyre's underlying fabrics and shares no data closure with any delegated estate
invariant no delegated estate implementation depends on Habitat
forbidden_inference Habitat reusing the relationship graph -> Habitat participating in institutional delegation
forbidden_inference this boundary existing -> an implementation being scheduled
